<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hindi strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "आप" with "-ें", and English loanwords where Hindi iOS uses them ("डिलीट", "सेटिंग").
  Hindi has the CLDR plural forms one and other; "one" also takes 0, so each form keeps the number.
  The duration chips have no unit, because "12–24 घंटे" is longer than 7 characters: the captions name the hours.
-->
